# LF everywhere: the platform has no Windows runtime target and deploys to
# Linux containers, so CRLF has no upside — it only bloats diffs when a
# whole-file rewrite normalizes endings as a side effect. text=auto lets git
# content-detect binaries (EDF fixtures, images) and leave them untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Kept from the earlier shell-script rule (shellcheck rejects CR after a
# shebang, SC1017); now redundant with the global rule but explicit is fine.
*.sh text eol=lf
